{
  "_comment": [
    "Curated SkillId -> equipped-Imagine table (issue #33). Hand-curated; do not",
    "regenerate blindly. Consumed by scripts/prep-imagine-icons.py and",
    "scripts/gen-imagine-table.py. See docs/packet-inspection.md.",
    "",
    "Derived from BPSR-ZDPS Data/SkillTable.json by taking every row whose",
    "SlotPositionId contains 7 or 8 (the reference's IsImagineSlot() predicate,",
    "DataTypes/SkillTable.cs:137-150), which yields 125 rows, then excluding 19",
    "false positives by hand (see _excluded).",
    "",
    "There is NO data-native predicate that reproduces this list: slotType,",
    "slotPassiveType and slotPositionId are identical (0 / 0 / [7,8]) across real",
    "Imagines and false positives alike, and skillType overlaps. An icon-path",
    "heuristic also fails - ids 2350, 2351, 2900370 and 2900570 carry genuine",
    "skill_aoyi icons but are not Imagines.",
    "",
    "IDENTITY IS THE ICON BASENAME, NOT THE NAME.",
    "",
    "Ids 3901-3987 are the canonical Imagine set: 83 ids covering 81 distinct",
    "icons and 81 distinct names, with icon and name bijective - no canonical",
    "icon serves two names. (3982/3986 and 3983/3987 are exact duplicate pairs,",
    "same icon and same name.) The remaining 23 ids are variants, and every one",
    "of their icons already appears in the canonical set - there are zero orphan",
    "icons. So a variant is always another id for a canonical Imagine.",
    "",
    "Three variants disagree with their canonical name and must NOT be treated as",
    "separate Imagines: 102651 'Boar Knight' and 102655 'Boar Impact!' are both",
    "the Boar Imagine ('Stunt! Boarrier Rush'), and 2002840 'Arcane! Swift Vortex'",
    "is 'Arcane! Meteor Shower'. Deduplicating by name would let a single equipped",
    "Imagine occupy both of a player's two slots. Deduplicate by icon, and display",
    "the canonical (39xx) name.",
    "",
    "All 106 ids are kept rather than just the canonical 83, because no packet",
    "capture exists to confirm whether the wire carries canonical or variant ids.",
    "Matching both is the safe choice; they collapse to the same identity anyway."
  ],
